{
 "note": "APPEND-ONLY successor. ARM-2 round-20 CORRECTIONS (Codex): round-19 fixed the training math but the image + calibration pipeline was not executable or secure. All six blocking findings fixed. F1 IMAGE WORKFLOW COULD NOT PUBLISH: the existing medzen-image-publisher-role trusts only model-images-publish.yml and grants only two ECR repos (AWS sim: implicitDeny for medzen-trainer-omniasr). NEW infra/trainer_image_publisher.tf = a dedicated non-deploy role trusting arm2-trainer-image.yml@master and scoped to ONLY medzen-trainer-omniasr; the workflow now uses the new var MEDZEN_TRAINER_IMAGE_PUBLISHER_ROLE_ARN. F2 COMMAND INJECTION: inputs.sha was interpolated into shell after creds; now it must be exactly 40-hex (validated first), reaches shell ONLY as the quoted $SHA env (no inline expressions in run blocks), and the checkout is proven to equal it BEFORE credentials are acquired. F3 CALIBRATION WRAPPER DID NOT EXIST: SageMaker ran pipeline.omniasr_train directly, writing serve=null/dev_wer=null so a real calibration always failed its verifier. NEW pipeline/omniasr_calibrate.py = the real entrypoint (train -> export -> readyz -> dev-sentinel WER -> finalize metrics -> run verifier -> exit nonzero on failure), fail-closed (a broken decode leaves serve/dev_wer unset -> verifier refuses -> job fails, never a false pass); the launcher renders this entrypoint for KD packets. WER is a pure host-tested word-level edit distance (no new image dep). F4 VERIFIER BYPASSABLE: the earlier check validated presence, not the canonical contract; Codex bypassed with a nonexistent script, a traversal artifact, expected_steps=1 vs 30, an enormous GPU ceiling and an empty dev-language list. BOTH load_verifier_spec AND validate_arm2_semantics now pin the canonical contract (script==scripts/verify_arm2_calibration.py, artifact==calibration-metrics.json, expected_steps==MEDZEN_MAX_STEPS, ceiling in 1..24GiB physical, dev langs non-empty subset of the preservation set including lingala+swahili), and the calibration env inputs (MEDZEN_CALIBRATION_PACKET, _SHA256, _DEV_SENTINEL_MANIFEST_FILES) are required. F5 EVIDENCE NOT BOUND: metrics now carry an identity block (run_fingerprint, training_job_name, export manifest/model sha, per-dev manifest sha, scorer, packet_sha256, verifier_script_sha256); the verifier binds metrics to THIS packet's canonical sha (launcher-injected, no self-reference) and to its own bytes; samples/sec is recorded; the loss equation total==ctc+alpha*kd and step contiguity 1..N are checked; and the metrics accumulator is persisted/restored across a checkpoint so a resumed run keeps the FULL trajectory (validated end-to-end with real torch: per_step contiguous 1..4 across a simulated reclaim). F6 IMAGE TESTS OMITTED: Dockerfile.trainer-omniasr now COPYs + RUNS tests/test_arm2_calibration.py and ships omniasr_calibrate.py + verify_arm2_calibration.py + the packet in both stages. Suite: 2432 passed / 0 failed WITH torch; CI-matching no-torch run re-confirmed. HONEST PREREQUISITES (like the image digest): the dev-sentinel slice manifests (platform/manifests/dev-sentinels/{lingala,swahili}.jsonl) must be authored+committed+COPYed into the image, and the wrapper's model-touching stages (readyz reload, CTC-greedy decode) are validated only in-image by arm2-trainer-image.yml. HOLDS UNCHANGED: NO Arm-2 compute, sealed data, promotion or deployment; digest pinned only after the native build passes, then the reviewer issues the approval.",
